{"conversation_id":"f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The Round-2 independent second-architect review has been written to [1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md).\n\n---\n\n# Round-2 Independent Second-Architect Review: Register-VM Wasm Lowering Plan (R2)\n\n- **Reviewed Plan**: [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md)\n- **Round-1 Review**: [1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md)\n- **Reviewer**: `gemini-4-argon` (Architect)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Round-1 Finding Resolution Audit (Verified Against Body \u0026 Source Code)\n\nEach of the seven Round-1 findings (`MAJOR-1`..`MAJOR-3`, `MINOR-1`..`MINOR-4`) was audited against both the body of [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) (not merely the §0 revision log) and the current implementation in `src/cljc/yin/vm/`.\n\n### MAJOR-1 — Empty-`K` `:return` and `:return-result` continuation restore `:pc` preservation\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §2.3 (`:return`, line 109), §2.4 (line 132), §3.2 step 5 (line 170), §6 W2 (line 265), §6 W3 (line 271).\n- **Verification**:\n  - [`return-value`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L428-L436): When `(:continuation state)` is `nil`, the transition produces `(assoc state :value retval :halted? true :parked? false)` while leaving `:pc` unchanged (`(:pc state)`, or `(:pc entry)` when driven from a `:return-result` restore).\n  - [`restore-continuation-record`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L455-L468): The `:return-result` branch restores `:pc (:pc entry)`, `:frames (:frames entry)`, `:continuation (:continuation entry)`, `:store-of (:store-of entry)`, and `:halted? false` onto `base` before calling `(return-value ... value)`.\n  - §2.3, §2.4, and §3.2 step 5 in the revised plan now specify this exact sequence and explicitly forbid clobbering `:pc` with `0` or advancing it on empty-`K` `:return`.\n\n### MAJOR-2 — Bidirectional synchronization between Clojure VM map fields and wasm linear memory across engine/public seams\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §1.2.1 (\"Mandatory map ↔ memory synchronization\", lines 52–61), §1.3 (line 67), §4.1 (line 186), §6 W0 (line 254), §6 W1 (line 259), §6 W3 (line 273).\n- **Verification**:\n  - [`module/gc-roots`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L944-L949) and [`collect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2587-L2614) during `:cell/new` ([engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2720)): `engine/handle-effect` on `:cell/new` collects live heap cells by walking Clojure keys (`:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:value`, `:store`, `:wait-set`, `:run-queue`, `:yin.k/puts`) on the `state` map passed to it.\n  - [`handle-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2746): Writes `:value` on `state'` and may update `:store`, `:id-counter`, `:wait-set`, `:run-queue`, `:parked?`, `:halted?`, and `:yin.k/*`.\n  - [register_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L444-L445): Callers mutate Clojure map keys (e.g., `(assoc vm3 :store {...})`) between public steps.\n  - §1.2.1 now mandates the three-point synchronization contract: (1) export hot wasm state (`:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:value`, `:halted?`, `:parked?`, `:store-of`) to the Clojure map before any `engine/*` call, (2) re-import any mutated Clojure map fields back into wasm state after `engine/*` returns, and (3) import caller-visible Clojure map keys on public entry (`vm/step`, `vm/run`, `vm/eval`, `restore-continuation`) and export before returning.\n\n### MAJOR-3 — `:call` `:host-fn` effect completion contract (`payload-of`, `park-entry-fns`, blocked `:pc` advance, post-effect `state` preservation)\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §2.3 (`:call`, line 106), §2.4 (\"Exact host-function effect completion\", lines 125–135), §6 W3 (line 271).\n- **Verification**:\n  - [`handle-host-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L533-L580), [register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L709-L719), and [`module/handle-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L579-L584):\n    - `payload-of` is constructed at the call site with `:pc (inc site-pc)` and `:reg dst`.\n    - `park-entry-fns` supplies `:stream/put`, `:stream/next`, and `:module/require` park entries, with `handle-host-effect` falling back to `(or (get park-entry-fns eff-type) (when (= :module/try-require eff-type) (:module/require park-entry-fns)) (when (= :stream/poll eff-type) (:stream/next park-entry-fns)))`.\n    - On `:blocked? true`, `handle-host-effect` returns `(assoc res-state :pc (inc site-pc))` without calling `return-result`.\n    - On `:parked? true`, `handle-host-effect` returns `res-state` directly.\n    - On `:halted? true`, `handle-host-effect` returns `(assoc res-state :value value)` directly.\n    - Otherwise, `return-result` writes `dst` or calls `return-value` on **`res-state`** (preserving all post-effect mutations to `:store`, `:id-counter`, `:wait-set`, `:run-queue`, `:yin.k/*`, etc.).\n  - §2.4 captures every branch and fallback rule faithfully.\n\n### MINOR-1 — Continuation invocation check order and foreign-continuation error keyword\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED (with code-verified correction from Astra)**\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §2.3 (`:call`, line 106), §3.2 (line 174), §6 W2 (line 265).\n- **Verification**:\n  - Astra's refutation of the error keyword in Round 1 is verified against [`engine/operator-kind`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L78-L95): `operator-kind` checks `(and (map? f) (= :continuation (:type f)))` and, when `(not= (:machine f) (:type state))`, throws `(ex-info \"Cannot invoke foreign continuation\" {:type :yin/uncaught-exception, :exception {:reason :foreign-value, :kind :continuation, ...}})`.\n  - Next, [register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L724) calls [`engine/continuation-argument`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L103-L112), which checks `(= 1 (count args))` and throws `:reason :continuation-arity`.\n  - Finally, [`check-format!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L730-L732) throws `\"Continuation format mismatch\"` with `{:expected fmt, :actual format}` on mismatch.\n  - §2.3, §3.2, and §6 W2 now state this exact three-step check order and exact error payloads.\n\n### MINOR-2 — `:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` must preserve existing `:registers`, `:frames`, and `:continuation`\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §2.3 (`:return` line 109, `:halt` line 110), §2.4 (line 132), §6 W1 (line 259).\n- **Verification**:\n  - [register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L432) and [register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L745-L747) preserve `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, and `:pc` unchanged on empty-`K` `:return` and `:halt`, only updating `:value`, `:halted? true`, and `:parked? false`.\n  - §2.3, §2.4, and §6 W1 now state this invariant explicitly.\n\n### MINOR-3 — `effects/wait-entry-defect` scope and custody gate (`:yin.k/gate`) preservation\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED (with two code-verified corrections from Astra)**\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §1.2 (line 45), §4.2 (line 198), §4.2.1 (\"Custody gates are preserved engine semantics\", lines 200–210), §4.3 (lines 215–216), §6 W3 (line 273), §6 W4 (line 279).\n- **Verification**:\n  - [`wait-entry-defect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L345-L384) validates queued `:wait-set` entries only (`:stream/put`, `:stream/next`, `:module/require`).\n  - Astra's two refutations of Round-1 wording details are verified against [engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc):\n    1. [`engine/issue-number`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L554-L559) increments `:yin.k/issued` (not `:yin.k/next-issue`) on `state` and stamps `:yin.k/issue n` on gated records.\n    2. [`engine/handle-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2713-L2716) on `:stream/close` calls [`gate-refuse!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L484-L492) (which refuses `:exporting` and `:ended`, returning `:running` when mode is `:running`) and then delegates to [`handle-close`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L744-L761), which under `:running` appends `{:stream-id stream-id, :yin.k/issue n}` to `:yin.k/closes` and returns `nil` without calling `stream/close!`.\n  - §4.2.1 accurately documents all four `:yin.k/*` state keys (`:yin.k/gate`, `:yin.k/puts`, `:yin.k/closes`, `:yin.k/issued`) and exact gate behavior across `:running`, `:exporting`, and `:ended`.\n\n### MINOR-4 — Module attachment base offsets, combined-segment payload reads, and empty-base rows\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §5 (lines 229, 232–234), §6 W4 (line 279).\n- **Verification**:\n  - [`attach-module-code`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L184-L227), [`shift-pool`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L135-L146), [`fetch-pool` / `fetch-instr`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L525-L530), and [debruijn_register_effects.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L97-L120):\n    - `attach-module-code` records `:base-code (count cur-code)` and `:base-pool (count cur-pool)` (so attaching to an empty base yields `{:base-code 0, :base-pool 0}`), shifts module pool `:code` (`+ base-code`) and `:consts` (`+ base-pool`) only when `(or (pos? base-code) (pos? base-pool))`, and increments `:program-version`.\n    - `fetch-pool` and `fetch-instr` index the combined `:pool` and `:bytecode` vectors at `(:pc state)`.\n  - §5 and §6 W4 now match this exact attachment and segment-indexing contract.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Full-Document Consistency \u0026 Regression Check\n\nA complete pass over §1–§7 of [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) confirmed:\n- No internal contradictions between the §0 revision log and the normative sections (§1–§7).\n- The W0–W6 phase gates (§6) incorporate all new synchronization, restore, effect-completion, custody-gate, and module-attachment invariants into concrete parity assertions.\n- No architectural drift or regressions were introduced during the Round-2 edits.\n\n---\n\n## Verdict\n\nAPPROVE\n\n### Findings Remaining\nNone. All 3 MAJOR and 4 MINOR findings from Round 1 have been completely and accurately resolved in the plan body.\n\n### Properties Passing Review\n1. **Execution Boundary \u0026 Dual-Tier Dispatch**: [`engine/run-loop`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2772-L2797) and [`step-on-stream`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L751-L775) cleanly accommodate a wasm inner hot-loop without forking scheduler, stream, store, or module state.\n2. **Bidirectional Clojure-Map ↔ Linear-Memory Synchronization**: Export-before-engine-call, re-import-after-engine-call, and public-boundary import/export (§1.2.1) preserve [`module/gc-roots`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L944-L949) during `:cell/new` GC collection ([engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2587-L2614)), preserve `:value` and store/scheduler updates after `engine/handle-effect`, and honor caller `assoc` mutations between steps.\n3. **Value Representation \u0026 Two-Level Memory Management**: The 64-bit NaN-boxed / tagged-handle value encoding and split between transient wasm arena allocations and Yin logical heap cells (`:heap`, `:cells`, `engine/collect`) preserve Clojure value equality and deterministic logical GC semantics.\n4. **Bytecode \u0026 Instruction Semantics**: All 18 opcodes ([`step-instruction`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L622-L749)), [`resolve-Access`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L477-L513), [`call-WithArgs`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L582-L620), [`return-value`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L428-L436), and [`handle-host-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L533-L580) match the canonical interpreter transition-for-transition, including empty-`K` `:pc` and `:registers`/`:frames`/`:continuation` preservation and post-effect `res-state` propagation.\n5. **Reified Continuations \u0026 Portable Format**: Continuation capture ([register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L241-L294)) and [`restore-continuation-record`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L455-L468) preserve `{:type :continuation, :machine :yin.vm/debruijn-register, :format :debruijn-register-v1, :value payload}` bit-for-bit across `:call`, `:park`, and `:return-result` entries, including the exact continuation-invocation validation order (`:foreign-value` -\u003e `:continuation-arity` -\u003e `\"Continuation format mismatch\"`).\n6. **FFI, Effect Handling, and Custody Gates**: Two-step `:ffi/call` ([register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L691-L705), [ffi.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc#L307-L351)), `debruijn_register_effects` validation ([`wait-entry-defect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L345-L384) on `:wait-set`), and `:yin.k/gate` custody semantics (`:yin.k/puts`, `:yin.k/closes`, `:yin.k/issued` across `:running`, `:exporting`, and `:ended` in [engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L484-L761)) are preserved unchanged.\n7. **Dynamic Module Attachment**: [`attach-module-code`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L184-L227) base-offset shifting, `:module-Table` recording (including `{:base-code 0, :base-pool 0}` on empty bases), combined-segment `:bytecode`/`:pool` indexing, and `:program-version` cache invalidation are preserved.\n8. **Phased Delivery \u0026 Parity Gates (W0–W6)**: Each phase maintains green `clj -M:test` and `bb test:cljs` suites and enforces state-equivalence against the canonical interpreter.\n","duration_seconds":1624.491027,"num_turns":3,"usage":{"input_tokens":465444,"output_tokens":4